{
  "id": "m10-min-stabbing",
  "title": "Fewest Pins",
  "source": {
    "name": "Classic interval stabbing / minimum arrows"
  },
  "rating": 1400,
  "tags": [
    "greedy",
    "intervals",
    "sorting"
  ],
  "statement": "You are given `n` closed intervals `[l_i, r_i]` on the number line with integer endpoints. A pin placed at an integer position `x` hits every interval with `l_i <= x <= r_i`. Print the fewest pins that hit every interval.\n\n**Input.** First line `n`. Then `n` lines `l_i r_i`.\n\n**Output.** The minimum number of pins.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ n ≤ 2000 in this browser version (the idea scales to 2·10^5)",
    "0 ≤ l_i ≤ r_i ≤ 10^9"
  ],
  "timeLimitMs": 2000,
  "hints": [
    "Think about the interval whose right end is smallest: where should a pin that hits it go?",
    "Putting the pin at its right end hits that interval and as many others as any other position could.",
    "Sort by right end. Keep `last` (the last pin). When an interval has `l > last`, place a new pin at its `r`."
  ],
  "editorial": "Sort by right endpoint. Consider the interval with the smallest right end `r`. Some pin must lie in it. Every other interval has right end `>= r`, so any interval hit by a pin at `x <= r` with `x >= l` of this interval is also hit by a pin at `r` whenever its left end is `<= r` (it contains `x` and extends to at least `r`). Moving the pin to `r` therefore never hurts (exchange argument). Place it, discard all intervals containing `r`, and repeat. Implementation: scan in sorted order and a new pin at `r` is needed exactly when `l > last`. Time `O(n log n)`. Touching intervals like `[1,3]` and `[3,5]` share the point 3, so one pin suffices.",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n log n)",
    "space": "O(n)"
  },
  "starter": {
    "python": "import sys\nd = sys.stdin.read().split()\nn = int(d[0])\niv = [(int(d[1 + 2 * i]), int(d[2 + 2 * i])) for i in range(n)]\n# sort by right end and sweep\n",
    "javascript": "const n = parseInt(readLine());\n// then n lines 'l r'\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        // then n pairs l r\n    }\n}\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int n; cin >> n;  // read n intervals; sort by right end\n    return 0;\n}\n"
  },
  "solutions": {
    "python": "import sys\nd = sys.stdin.read().split()\nn = int(d[0])\niv = sorted((int(d[2 + 2 * i]), int(d[1 + 2 * i])) for i in range(n))  # (right, left)\nlast = None\ncnt = 0\nfor r, l in iv:\n    if last is None or l > last:\n        cnt += 1\n        last = r\nprint(cnt)\n",
    "javascript": "const lines = [];\nlet line;\nwhile ((line = readLine()) !== null) lines.push(line);\nconst tok = lines.join(' ').split(/\\s+/).filter(s => s.length);\nconst n = Number(tok[0]);\nconst iv = [];\nfor (let i = 0; i < n; i++) iv.push([Number(tok[2 + 2 * i]), Number(tok[1 + 2 * i])]);\niv.sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0]);\nlet last = null, cnt = 0;\nfor (const [r, l] of iv) {\n  if (last === null || l > last) {\n    cnt++;\n    last = r;\n  }\n}\nconsole.log(cnt);\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        long[][] iv = new long[n][2];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            iv[i][1] = sc.nextLong();\n            iv[i][0] = sc.nextLong();\n        }\n        Arrays.sort(iv, (a, b) -> Long.compare(a[0], b[0]));\n        long last = Long.MIN_VALUE;\n        int cnt = 0;\n        for (long[] x : iv) {\n            if (x[1] > last) {\n                cnt++;\n                last = x[0];\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(cnt);\n    }\n}\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<pair<long long, long long>> iv(n);\n    for (auto &x : iv) cin >> x.second >> x.first;  // stored as (right, left)\n    sort(iv.begin(), iv.end());\n    long long last = LLONG_MIN;\n    int cnt = 0;\n    for (auto &x : iv) {\n        if (x.second > last) {\n            cnt++;\n            last = x.first;\n        }\n    }\n    cout << cnt << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n"
  },
